***********
version 1.0
***********

initial release:
- Git::GitRepository class for repository operations (open, init, and
  genuinely in-memory virtual repositories)
- index/staging operations (add, remove, reset)
- commit creation and history traversal
- branch and tag management
- diff and status operations
- remote management (fetch, push, pull)
- merge with conflict detection
- stash, blame, config operations
- revision walking with sorting
- git transport authentication delegated to libgit2 (SSH agent, credential
  helpers); credentials are never stored or logged by this module
- sandboxing support (QDOM_FILESYSTEM, QDOM_NETWORK)
- cooperative cancellation for blocking operations
- GitDataProvider module for data provider integration
- GitConnections module for connection management
- GitConfigManager module for high-level configuration management
- GitConfigWatcher with observer pattern for change detection
- GitForgeHelper module for GitHub/GitLab PR/MR creation

security and robustness:
- createVirtual() repositories are fully in-memory with no filesystem
  footprint; a 0700 temp repo (honoring TMPDIR) is created transparently
  only when a remote is added, and is reclaimed at module unload
- file paths are validated against absolute-path and ".." traversal; disk
  writes use O_NOFOLLOW to defeat working-tree symlink attacks
- remote URLs reject the "ext::" arbitrary-command transport
- fetch()/push() hold the repository lock across network I/O
- when a SandboxManager is active, fetch()/push()/pull()/connectRemote()
  run a best-effort network pre-flight that resolves the remote host and
  validates each address against the network security policy (SSRF /
  private-network / cloud-metadata blocking) before connecting
- GitForgeHelper validates the GitLab URL before attaching the API token
  and scrubs credential context from REST errors
- GitConnections rejects ".." in gitlocal:// URLs

GitDataProvider:
- the log and diff action responses now use typed sub-types
  (commit/signature/diff-entry) instead of untyped lists, so the UI
  exposes per-field mapping
- the diff and log actions preselect their options so the action form
  is populated
